          "source": "",
          "thread": "Danny Ryan leadership vacuum",
          "why": "His departure after seven years and the community's vocal push for him to lead the EF made readers hungry for every response and counter-response in the saga."
        },
        {
          "source": "",
          "thread": "Aya and EF toxicity backlash",
          "why": "The weekend pile-on against Aya Miyaguchi and the EF triggered rare public interventions from both Danny Ryan and Vitalik, giving readers a live governance crisis to follow."
        },
        {
          "source": "",
          "thread": "EF treasury ETH selling",
          "why": "Suspicion that the foundation was quietly dumping ETH onto the market, combined with a provocative $fxUSD alternative and Justin Drake's defence of the practice, created a charged financial accountability story."
        },
        {
          "source": "",
          "thread": "EigenLayer conflicts of interest",
          "why": "Disclosure that EF researchers received significant EigenLayer token incentives raised direct questions about whether the foundation could remain a neutral steward of Ethereum."
        },
        {
          "source": "",
          "thread": "Ethereum competitiveness crisis",
          "why": "Bitcoin and Solana outperforming ETH while L2s fragmented value and a core developer called crypto a 'value-extracting casino' fed a narrative that the EF had lost strategic focus."
        },
        {
          "source": "",
          "thread": "ZK L2 grants and Dencun upgrade",
          "why": "The $900K ZK grants initiative and Dencun hard fork gave readers a counterweight — concrete infrastructure wins to weigh against the governance noise."
        }
      ]
    },
